"A baby's skin is very soft.": "fca71634b522",
"A helmet protects your head.": "4aaaae39d6ae",
"How does sweat help you cool down?": "272a423fb0fe",
"I got a bad sunburn at the beach.": "0b6afb341044",
"Put on sunscreen before you go outside.": "41f7cf0f18da",
"Scientists measure the strength of UV with the UV index. When it is 3 or higher, you need protection, and in Taiwan it often goes above 10 on summer days around noon. A simple test: if your shadow is shorter than you are, the sun is strong. Wear a hat, cover up, look for shade, and use sunscreen. Now check how strong the sun is in Changhua today with the tool below the model.": "b2e5b0320087",
"Skin also helps control your temperature. You have between 2 and 4 million sweat glands. On a hot day, they pour sweat onto your skin, and as the sweat evaporates, it carries heat away. The blood vessels near the surface also widen to let heat out, which is why you look red after running. When you are cold, those blood vessels narrow, and tiny muscles pull your hairs upright, giving you goosebumps.": "f16be09c1f21",
"Skin has three layers. The top layer, the epidermis, is thinner than a sheet of paper on most of your body. Its outside is made of flat, dead cells that flake off all the time, and new cells from below replace the whole layer about once a month. Under it is the dermis, a thicker, stretchy layer that holds blood vessels, nerves, sweat glands, and the roots of your hairs. At the bottom is a layer of fat that works like a cushion and a warm blanket.": "338cff7d9673",
"Sunlight is good for skin in small amounts, because skin uses it to make vitamin D, which you need for strong bones. But sunlight also carries ultraviolet light, or UV, which you cannot see. To protect itself, skin makes a dark substance called melanin, and a tan is a sign that your skin has already been harmed by UV. Too much UV causes sunburn, and over many years it can lead to wrinkles and skin cancer.": "f413fd8a8280",
