"Why is a tan not a sign of healthy skin?": "399c3543a206",
"Your skin is full of sensors. Some feel a light touch, some feel a hard press, and others feel heat, cold, itching, and pain. Your fingertips and lips have the most, which is why you read with your fingertips when you feel for something in the dark. Your fingertips also have ridges called fingerprints. They formed before you were born, and no two people have the same ones, not even identical twins.": "e5b46680dcb6",
"Your skin is your body's biggest organ. Spread out flat, an adult's skin would cover about 2 square meters, about the size of a single bed. It is waterproof, it stretches, and it repairs itself when you get a scrape. Most importantly, it is a wall that keeps germs, dirt, and harmful chemicals outside your body, and it keeps the water inside your body from drying out.": "eaefe60503e1",
